@@ -16,11 +16,31 @@ uv run python run.py invoice_processing --limit 5
 
 The default model is `typesafe:jev-1.13.0`. Override it with `--model provider:model`
 using the provider's exact model ID, such as `--model openai:gpt-6-astra`. Supported
-providers: `openai`, `anthropic`, `fireworks`, `groq`, `cerebras`, and `typesafe`.
+providers: `openai`, `anthropic`, `fireworks`, `groq`, `cerebras`, `typesafe`, and `typical`.
 For example, `fireworks:accounts/fireworks/models/glm-5p3`. Set the matching
 provider's `*_API_KEY` environment variable. TypeSafe's model is
 `typesafe:jev-1.13.0`; it uses the public API endpoint unless `--base-url` overrides it.
 
+The `typical` provider runs a self-hosted Typical model through the native TypeSafe
+client protocol without identifying it as Jev:
+
+```bash
+export TYPICAL_API_KEY=your-local-endpoint-key
+export TYPICAL_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8090
+uv run python run.py invoice_processing \
+  --model typical:typical-r050-sha256-0123456789abcdef \
+  --name typical-r050-invoices
+```
+
+Use a literal, immutable model identifier after `typical:`. The endpoint must return
+that exact identifier in `response.model`; aliases or silently substituted models are
+rejected. `--base-url` can replace `TYPICAL_BASE_URL`, but one of them is required.
+Set it to the host root: the SDK appends `/v1/systemone`, so do not append `/v1`.
+Typical reads only `TYPICAL_API_KEY`, never `TYPESAFE_API_KEY`, and defaults to
+`--questions all --thinking off`. No Typical prices are assumed: costs remain unknown
+until measured rates are deliberately added to `core/pricing.json`. Typical calls
+disable SDK retries so endpoint failures remain visible in benchmark results.
+
 `core/pricing.json` uses the same exact `provider:model` keys. Missing rates produce
 unknown cost.
 
